One more recommendation

To make this portfolio genuinely stand out in 2026, don't stop at "everything moves on scroll." Many portfolios already do that.

Instead, make the scroll itself tell a narrative. Treat the site like a directed experience:

Act I — Introduction: Introduce yourself with bold typography and a cinematic entrance.
Act II — Craft: Reveal how you think, design, and engineer software through interactive visualizations rather than paragraphs.
Act III — Projects: Each project becomes its own immersive scene with animations tied to scroll progress.
Act IV — Proof: Show measurable impact—performance improvements, architecture diagrams, GitHub activity, before/after metrics, and case studies.
Act V — Contact: End with a memorable interaction that makes reaching out feel like completing the journey.

The strongest developer portfolios don't just demonstrate animation skill—they communicate engineering quality, performance discipline, product thinking, and storytelling all at once.